{# Shared deny contexts - the OpenLiteSpeed counterpart of the nginx
   templates' `location ... { deny all; }` blocks, kept in one file so the two
   backends cannot drift apart in what they protect.

   These are additions on top of OPanel's configuration, not a replacement for
   any of it: OPanel's rewrite blocks are left exactly as they are, because
   measurement showed they work (WordPress permalinks resolve, and a real file
   still bypasses the front controller, so RewriteCond is honoured).

   The one thing that does not work is the `[F]` flag: OPanel's
   `RewriteRule ^xmlrpc\.php$ - [F,L]` does not deny on this build - a POST to
   xmlrpc.php answered 200 with the full XML-RPC method list while every other
   rule in the same block was demonstrably firing. An accessControl context
   does return 403.

   Two details, both measured rather than assumed:
   - A regex context whose pattern is not anchored at the end is treated as a
     directory: `^/\.(?!well-known)` made /.htaccess answer 301 to
     /.htaccess/ instead of 403. Anchoring with `.*$` fixes it.
   - The negative lookahead is honoured, so /.well-known/acme-challenge keeps
     serving - which SSL issuance depends on.

   These must be emitted BEFORE `context /` so the more specific match wins. #}
{% for blocked in exact_denied | default([]) %}
context {{ blocked }} {
    location              {{ root_path }}/{{ document_root }}{{ blocked }}
    accessControl {
        deny              ALL
    }
}

{% endfor %}
{% for pattern in regex_denied | default([]) %}
context exp:{{ pattern }} {
    accessControl {
        deny              ALL
    }
}

{% endfor %}
